/*
description: |
    Settings shared by every LYGIA Metal file. Included by each .msl, so
    including any LYGIA function brings it in.

    LYGIA_FNC is the qualifier in front of every function definition. By
    default it's `static inline`: each .metal file that includes LYGIA gets
    its own copy, so several .metal files in one target link without duplicate
    symbols, and each file can set its own options (FBM_OCTAVES, ...).

    To compile LYGIA once as a helper library that other files call, define
    LYGIA_FNC as empty before including LYGIA, so the functions are exported:

        #define LYGIA_FNC
        #include "lygia/generative/fbm.msl"

    The callers then declare the functions they use and link against that
    library (static, dynamic, or its .air). Its options are fixed when it's
    built.
*/

#ifndef LYGIA_FNC
#define LYGIA_FNC static inline
#endif
